    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offensive engine is anchored today by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Jackson Merrill** (72.01), who represent our clearest paths to high-output production. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from an elite environment against Buehler, bolstered by a +16% park factor and favorable wind conditions, while **Jackson Merrill** leverages a high stolen base probability due to a slow-delivery opposing pitcher. Both **Kyle Tucker** (71.48) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (70.52) also grade out as strong starts, with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** providing significant value as a top-order spark against Hancock. These players are prioritized for their ability to catalyze the 5x5 categories, particularly with the scarcity of stolen bases keeping speed-centric threats in the starting slots.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved **Wade Meckler** (45.25), who landed just outside our effective scoring threshold. While **Wade Meckler** carries an appealing profile, the optimization model favored the slightly higher ceiling of **Dominic Smith** (47.44) and **Miguel Vargas** (45.72), largely due to their specific lineup placement and platoon advantages. We are closely monitoring the risk profile of **Liam Hicks** (41.15); while he retains a starting role, his matchup against Skenes is a significant drag on his efficiency, serving as a reminder to be cautious with the game cap when facing elite-tier pitching. As we navigate the schedule, the health status of **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Jorge Polanco** remains a primary concern for our long-term depth, leaving us reliant on current starters to maintain our competitive edge in stolen bases and counting stats.",
